[E-NO-READING] Error: this test fact can't be taken apart with a tuple pattern
   ╭─[ reject/proof-tuple-test-fact-no-reading.sw:6:5 ]
   │
 6 │   | (x, _) => x
   │     ───┬──  
   │        ╰──── `a && b = False` reads as `a = False ∨ b = False` (`Bool.andReadsFalse`)
   │ 
   │ Note 1: a test fact can always be matched by a name, and `.read` gives the proposition
   │ 
   │ Note 2: a tuple pattern takes apart a proof of `∧` or `∃`, and this test fact's reading isn't one
   │ 
   │ Note 3: this statement is false; a counterexample:
   │           a = True
   │           b = False
   │         `(a && b) = False` holds
   │         `a = False` is false:
   │           left:  True
   │           right: False
